<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#galley">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galley</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as galleys</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A galley is a warship propelled mainly by oars, dominant in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> warfare for centuries. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>'s ocean-going sailing ships carrying heavy artillery gave it a decisive advantage in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> against opponents who relied on oar-powered galleys poorly suited to open-ocean conditions.</p></div>
